text: ['Add {B}{B}{B}.', "All creatures gain fear until end of turn. (They can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)\\nCycling {1}{B} ({1}{B}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Dirge of Dread, you may have target creature gain fear until end of turn.", 'Any player may have Browbeat deal 5 damage to them. If no one does, target player draws three cards.', "As Primal Clay enters the battlefield, it becomes your choice of a 3/3 artifact creature, a 2/2 artifact creature with flying, or a 1/6 Wall artifact creature with defender in addition to its other types. (A creature with defender can't attack.)", 'As Vesuvan Shapeshifter enters the battlefield or is turned face up, you may choose another creature on the battlefield. If you do, until Vesuvan Shapeshifter is turned face down, it becomes a copy of that creature, except it has "At the beginning of your upkeep, you may turn this creature face down."\\nMorph {1}{U}', "At the beginning of each opponent's end step, if you didn't lose life this turn, you may put a quest counter on Luminarch Ascension. (Damage causes loss of life.)\\n{1}{W}: Create a 4/4 white Angel creature token with flying. Activate only if Luminarch Ascension has four or more quest counters on it.", "At the beginning of your end step, if Erg Raiders didn't attack this turn, Erg Raiders deals 2 damage to you unless it came under your control this turn.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, choose one —\\n• Each player with exactly 13 life loses the game, then each player gains 1 life.\\n• Each player with exactly 13 life loses the game, then each player loses 1 life.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token.\\n{T}: Tap all untapped Wolf creatures you control. Each Wolf tapped this way deals damage equal to its power to target creature. That creature deals damage equal to its power divided as its controller chooses among any number of those Wolves.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you gain 1 life.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you lose 1 life unless an opponent has 10 or less life.', 'Attacking creatures get +2/+0 until end of turn.', "Blightning deals 3 damage to target player or planeswalker. That player or that planeswalker's controller discards two cards.", 'Chalice of the Void enters the battlefield with X charge counters on it.\\nWhenever a player casts a spell with mana value equal to the number of charge counters on Chalice of the Void, counter that spell.', "Chandra's Outrage deals 4 damage to target creature and 2 damage to that creature's controller.", 'Choose one —\\n• Boros Charm deals 4 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\n• Permanents you control gain indestructible until end of turn.\\n• Target creature gains double strike until end of turn.', 'Choose one —\\n• Counter target blue spell.\\n• Destroy target blue permanent.', 'Choose one —\\n• Counter target red spell.\\n• Destroy target red permanent.', 'Cinder Storm deals 7 damage to any target.', 'Counter target creature spell.\\nDraw a card.', 'Counter target spell.', "Counter target spell. Its controller may draw up to two cards at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.\\nYou draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Counter target spell.\\nAt the beginning of your next upkeep, pay {3}{U}{U}. If you don't, you lose the game.", 'Create X 4/4 white Angel creature tokens with flying.\\nCycling {2}{W} ({2}{W}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Decree of Justice, you may pay {X}. If you do, create X 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens.', 'Create three 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.', "Creatures with power greater than the number of cards in your hand can't attack.", "Creatures you control have menace. (They can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", 'Cycling {2}{G} ({2}{G}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Krosan Tusker, you may search your library for a basic land card, reveal that card, put it into your hand, then shuffle. (Do this before you draw.)', 'Damage that would reduce your life total to less than 1 reduces it to 1 instead.\\nMorph {R}{R} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'Deathtouch\\nMorph—Reveal a black card in your hand. (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Ruthless Ripper is turned face up, target player loses 2 life.', "Defender\\n{1}{U}: Returned Phalanx can attack this turn as though it didn't have defender.", "Defender\\n{T}: Exchange your life total with Tree of Redemption's toughness.", 'Destroy all artifacts, creatures, and enchantments.\\nCycling {3} ({3}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', "Destroy all creatures you don't control. They can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy all lands.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', "Destroy target artifact or land. It can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target creature with flying.', 'Destroy target creature.', 'Destroy target creature. Its owner gains 4 life.', 'Destroy target permanent.', 'Double strike', 'Draw a card for each tapped creature target opponent controls.', 'Draw a card, then draw cards equal to the number of cards named Accumulated Knowledge in all graveyards.', 'Draw three cards, then discard a card.', 'Draw three cards, then put two cards from your hand on top of your library in any order.', 'Each player exiles all creature cards from their graveyard, then sacrifices all creatures they control, then puts all cards they exiled this way onto the battlefield.', 'Enchant Forest\\nAs Utopia Sprawl enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\nWhenever enchanted Forest is tapped for mana, its controller adds an additional one mana of the chosen color.', "Enchant Island\\n{2}: Enchanted Island becomes a 3/2 blue Spirit creature with flying until end of turn. It's still a land.\\nWhen enchanted Island is put into a graveyard, you may return Genju of the Falls from your graveyard to your hand.", "Enchant Mountain\\n{2}: Enchanted Mountain becomes a 6/1 red Spirit creature until end of turn. It's still a land.\\nWhen enchanted Mountain is put into a graveyard, you may return Genju of the Spires from your graveyard to your hand.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can\'t attack or block.\\nEnchanted creature has "At the beginning of your upkeep, you lose 1 life."', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+0 and has trample.\\nWhen Rancor is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, return Rancor to its owner's hand.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and has "{1}, Sacrifice a permanent: This creature gains flying until end of turn."', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has "{T}: Create a 1/1 green Elf Warrior creature token."', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has "{T}: This creature deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker. You draw a card."', 'Enchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on it. Then if it has three or more +1/+1 counters on it, sacrifice Ordeal of Heliod.\\nWhen you sacrifice Ordeal of Heliod, you gain 10 life.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature deals damage to an opponent, you may draw a card.', 'Enchant creature\\n{U}: Tap enchanted creature.\\n{U}: Untap enchanted creature.', 'Enchant land\\nEnchanted land has "{T}: Target player loses 3 life."', 'Equipped creature doesn\'t untap during its controller\'s untap step.\\nEquipped creature has "{T}: This creature deals 2 damage to any target."\\nEquip {4}', 'Equipped creature gets +1/+1.\\nWhenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, you may attach Sai of the Shinobi to it.\\nEquip {2}', "Equipped creature has hexproof and haste. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\nEquip {1}", 'Exile Simian Spirit Guide from your hand: Add {R}.', 'Exile target creature you control, then return that card to the battlefield under your control.', 'Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.', "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may search your library for a Rat card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.", "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)\\nNezumi Cutthroat can't block.", "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)\\nWhenever Shadowmage Infiltrator deals combat damage to a player, you may draw a card.", 'First strike\\nNoncreature spells cost {1} more to cast.', "Flash\\nFlying\\nWhen Vendilion Clique enters the battlefield, look at target player's hand. You may choose a nonland card from it. If you do, that player reveals the chosen card, puts it on the bottom of their library, then draws a card.", 'Flash\\nIf an opponent would draw a card except the first one they draw in each of their draw steps, instead that player skips that draw and you draw a card.', 'Flash\\nWhen Mystic Snake enters the battlefield, counter target spell.', "Flash\\nWhen Whitemane Lion enters the battlefield, return a creature you control to its owner's hand.", 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{B}: Regenerate Will-o'-the-Wisp. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", 'Flying, first strike, vigilance, trample, haste, protection from black and from red', 'Flying, first strike\\nIf a source would deal damage to an opponent or a permanent an opponent controls, that source deals double that damage to that player or permanent instead.\\nIf a source would deal damage to you or a permanent you control, prevent half that damage, rounded up.', 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Nicol Bolas unless you pay {U}{B}{R}.\\nWhenever Nicol Bolas deals damage to an opponent, that player discards their hand.', 'Flying\\nIslandcycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for an Island card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', 'Flying\\nSacrifice a creature: Fallen Angel gets +2/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nWhen Bloodhunter Bat enters the battlefield, target player loses 2 life and you gain 2 life.', 'Flying\\nWhen Cloudblazer enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life and draw two cards.', "Flying\\nWhen Death's-Head Buzzard dies, all creatures get -1/-1 until end of turn.", 'Flying\\nWhen Squadron Hawk enters the battlefield, you may search your library for up to three cards named Squadron Hawk, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Flying\\nWhenever another creature dies, you may draw a card. If you do, discard a card.', 'Flying\\nWhenever another creature enters the battlefield under your control, Griffin Protector gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nWhenever you draw a card, Niv-Mizzet, the Firemind deals 1 damage to any target.\\n{T}: Draw a card.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Target attacking or blocking creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{U}{U}{U}: Regenerate Ghost Ship.', 'Gain control of target creature until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn. (It can attack and {T} this turn.)', "Grenzo, Dungeon Warden enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{2}: Put the bottom card of your library into your graveyard. If it's a creature card with power less than or equal to Grenzo's power, put it onto the battlefield.", 'Haste\\n{R}, {T}: Exile target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard.\\n{1}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice Izzet Chemister: Cast any number of cards exiled with Izzet Chemister without paying their mana costs.', "If you control a Forest, rather than pay this spell's mana cost, you may have an opponent gain 3 life.\\nTarget creature gets +4/+4 until end of turn.", 'Kindle deals X damage to any target, where X is 2 plus the number of cards named Kindle in all graveyards.', "Lifelink\\n{R}, {T}, Sacrifice another creature: Brion Stoutarm deals damage equal to the sacrificed creature's power to target player or planeswalker.", 'Lightning Bolt deals 3 damage to any target.', 'Look at the top five cards of your library. You may reveal a colorless card from among them and put it into your hand. Then put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', 'Megamorph {1}{G} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its megamorph cost and put a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nWhen Ainok Survivalist is turned face up, destroy target artifact or enchantment an opponent controls.', "Menace (This creature can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)\\nMegamorph {R} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its megamorph cost and put a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nWhen Ire Shaman is turned face up, exile the top card of your library. Until end of turn, you may play that card.", "Mogg Flunkies can't attack or block alone.", 'Morph {1}{U} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Willbender is turned face up, change the target of target spell or ability with a single target.', "Morph {3}{W}{W} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Karona's Zealot is turned face up, all damage that would be dealt to it this turn is dealt to target creature instead.", 'Morph {5}{G} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'Morph {5}{U}{U} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Brine Elemental is turned face up, each opponent skips their next untap step.', 'Morph {6}{G}{G} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', "Morph—Return two Islands you control to their owner's hand. (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Fathom Seer is turned face up, draw two cards.", "Morph—Reveal a blue card in your hand. (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Dragon's Eye Savants is turned face up, look at target opponent's hand.", 'Myriad Landscape enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Myriad Landscape: Search your library for up to two basic land cards that share a land type, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "Mystic of the Hidden Way can't be blocked.\\nMorph {2}{U} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)", "Nettle Sentinel doesn't untap during your untap step.\\nWhenever you cast a green spell, you may untap Nettle Sentinel.", 'Nonbasic lands are Mountains.', 'Other creatures you control get +1/+1.', 'Play with the top card of your library revealed.\\nYou may play lands from the top of your library.\\nLandfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life.', 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Protection from red\\nWhenever a player casts a red spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Protection from white', 'Protection from white and from black\\nWhenever you cast a creature spell, put a +1/+1 counter on Animar, Soul of Elements.\\nCreature spells you cast cost {1} less to cast for each +1/+1 counter on Animar.', "Put target nonland permanent on top of its owner's library.", 'Pyroclasm deals 2 damage to each creature.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nAs long as you control a red permanent, Ember Weaver gets +1/+0 and has first strike.', 'Relentless Rats gets +1/+1 for each other creature on the battlefield named Relentless Rats.\\nA deck can have any number of cards named Relentless Rats.', 'Return target card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Sacrifice Cursecatcher: Counter target instant or sorcery spell unless its controller pays {1}.', 'Sacrifice a creature: Phyrexian Ghoul gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Search your library and graveyard for five cards and exile the rest. Put the chosen cards on top of your library in any order. You lose half your life, rounded up.', 'Search your library for a creature card, reveal that card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', "Search your library for a green creature card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.\\nAt the beginning of your next upkeep, pay {2}{G}{G}. If you don't, you lose the game.", 'Search your library for a white card, a blue card, a black card, a red card, and a green card. Reveal those cards, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for up to two basic land cards, reveal those cards, put one onto the battlefield tapped and the other into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Skeletonize deals 3 damage to target creature. When a creature dealt damage this way dies this turn, create a 1/1 black Skeleton creature token with "{B}: Regenerate this creature."', "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)\\nCycling—Pay 2 life. (Pay 2 life, Discard this card: Draw a card.)", "Switch target creature's power and toughness until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.", 'Tap up to four target creatures.\\nCycling {1}{U} ({1}{U}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Choking Tethers, you may tap target creature.', 'Target creature and all other creatures with the same name as that creature get +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +1/+1 and gains double strike until end of turn. (It deals both first-strike and regular combat damage.)', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn.', "Target creature you control gains protection from the color of your choice until end of turn. (It can't be blocked, targeted, dealt damage, enchanted, or equipped by anything of that color.)\\nScry 1.", "Target creature you control gets +1/+2 until end of turn. It fights target creature you don't control. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)", "Target player draws X cards. Shuffle Blue Sun's Zenith into its owner's library.", 'Target player gains 2 life for each creature on the battlefield.', 'Target player sacrifices a creature.', "This spell can't be countered.\\nFlying, trample, protection from white and from blue\\n{R}: Akroma, Angel of Fury gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\nMorph {3}{R}{R}{R} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)", 'Thresher Lizard gets +1/+2 as long as you have one or fewer cards in hand.', 'Timberpack Wolf gets +1/+1 for each other creature you control named Timberpack Wolf.', "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)\\nHaste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nAt the beginning of the end step, sacrifice Ball Lightning.", 'Trample\\nWhen Iwamori of the Open Fist enters the battlefield, each opponent may put a legendary creature card from their hand onto the battlefield.', "Trample\\nWhenever a source deals damage to Phyrexian Obliterator, that source's controller sacrifices that many permanents.", 'Trample\\nWhenever an opponent gains life, put that many +1/+1 counters on Kavu Predator.', 'Trample\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, put a +1/+1 counter on Pyre Hound.', 'Untap target creature. It gets +2/+2 until end of turn and can block an additional creature this turn.', 'Until end of turn, target creature gains "{T}: Return target nonland permanent to its owner\'s hand."', 'Until end of turn, target creature gets +2/+0 and gains "When this creature dies, return it to the battlefield tapped under its owner\'s control."', 'Vigilance, reach\\nRuric Thar, the Unbowed attacks each combat if able.\\nWhenever a player casts a noncreature spell, Ruric Thar deals 6 damage to that player.', 'Vigilance\\nPlainscycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for a Plains card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', 'Vigilance\\nWhen Court Hussar enters the battlefield, look at the top three cards of your library, then put one of them into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.\\nWhen Court Hussar enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless {W} was spent to cast it.', 'When Ambassador Oak enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 green Elf Warrior creature token.', 'When Auramancer enters the battlefield, you may return target enchantment card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Balduvian Horde enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you discard a card at random.', 'When Baloth Null enters the battlefield, return up to two target creature cards from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Dusk Legion Zealot enters the battlefield, you draw a card and you lose 1 life.', 'When Enthralling Victor enters the battlefield, gain control of target creature an opponent controls with power 2 or less until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn. (It can attack and {T} this turn.)', "When Fiend Hunter enters the battlefield, you may exile another target creature.\\nWhen Fiend Hunter leaves the battlefield, return the exiled card to the battlefield under its owner's control.", 'When Fierce Empath enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a creature card with mana value 6 or greater, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Imperial Recruiter enters the battlefield, search your library for a creature card with power 2 or less, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Kavu Climber enters the battlefield, draw a card.', "When Laquatus's Champion enters the battlefield, target player loses 6 life.\\nWhen Laquatus's Champion leaves the battlefield, that player gains 6 life.\\n{B}: Regenerate Laquatus's Champion.", 'When Loyal Sentry blocks a creature, destroy that creature and Loyal Sentry.', "When Man-o'-War enters the battlefield, return target creature to its owner's hand.", "When Mesmeric Fiend enters the battlefield, target opponent reveals their hand and you choose a nonland card from it. Exile that card.\\nWhen Mesmeric Fiend leaves the battlefield, return the exiled card to its owner's hand.", 'When Perilous Myr dies, it deals 2 damage to any target.', 'When Phantasmal Bear becomes the target of a spell or ability, sacrifice it.', 'When Prophetic Prism enters the battlefield, draw a card.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'When Protean Hulk dies, search your library for any number of creature cards with total mana value 6 or less, put them onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'When Ravenous Chupacabra enters the battlefield, destroy target creature an opponent controls.', 'When Reef Worm dies, create a 3/3 blue Fish creature token with "When this creature dies, create a 6/6 blue Whale creature token with \'When this creature dies, create a 9/9 blue Kraken creature token.\'"', 'When Rest in Peace enters the battlefield, exile all graveyards.\\nIf a card or token would be put into a graveyard from anywhere, exile it instead.', 'When Self-Assembler enters the battlefield, you may search your library for an Assembly-Worker creature card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Stangg enters the battlefield, create Stangg Twin, a legendary 3/4 red and green Human Warrior creature token. Exile that token when Stangg leaves the battlefield. Sacrifice Stangg when that token leaves the battlefield.', 'When Sundering Titan enters or leaves the battlefield, choose a land of each basic land type, then destroy those lands.', 'When Treasure Keeper dies, reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a nonland card with mana value 3 or less. You may cast that card without paying its mana cost. Put all revealed cards not cast this way on the bottom of your library in a random order.', 'When Urbis Protector enters the battlefield, create a 4/4 white Angel creature token with flying.', 'When a creature you control dies, sacrifice Promise of Bunrei. If you do, create four 1/1 colorless Spirit creature tokens.', 'When you cast this spell, create X 0/1 red Kobold creature tokens named Kobolds of Kher Keep, where X is the amount of mana spent to cast it.\\nFlying\\nSacrifice another creature: Prossh, Skyraider of Kher gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Broodhatch Nantuko is dealt damage, you may create that many 1/1 green Insect creature tokens.\\nMorph {2}{G} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', "Whenever Frenzied Goblin attacks, you may pay {R}. If you do, target creature can't block this turn.", 'Whenever Jackal Pup is dealt damage, it deals that much damage to you.', 'Whenever Skirk Commando deals combat damage to a player, you may have it deal 2 damage to target creature that player controls.\\nMorph {2}{R} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'Whenever Zulaport Cutthroat or another creature you control dies, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Whenever a creature you control deals combat damage to a player, you may draw a card.\\n{1}{U}, {T}: Creatures your opponents control attack this turn if able.', 'Whenever a player casts a spell with mana value 3 or less, Eidolon of the Great Revel deals 2 damage to that player.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell that targets only Zada, Hedron Grinder, copy that spell for each other creature you control that the spell could target. Each copy targets a different one of those creatures.', 'Whenever you cycle or discard another card, Horror of the Broken Lands gets +2/+1 until end of turn.\\nCycling {B} ({B}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Whenever you draw a card, put a +1/+1 counter on Lorescale Coatl.', "Whenever you're dealt damage, you may create that many 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens.", 'You draw three cards and you lose 3 life.', 'You gain 6 life.\\nCycling {1}{W} ({1}{W}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Renewed Faith, you may gain 2 life.', 'You may play two additional lands on each of your turns.', 'You may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield. If you do, sacrifice it unless you pay its mana cost reduced by up to {2}.', 'You may reveal a creature or land card you own from outside the game and put it into your hand. Exile Living Wish.', "[+2]: Look at the top card of target player's library. You may put that card on the bottom of that player's library.\\n[0]: Draw three cards, then put two cards from your hand on top of your library in any order.\\n[−1]: Return target creature to its owner's hand.\\n[−12]: Exile all cards from target player's library, then that player shuffles their hand into their library.", '{1}{B}, Discard a card: Return Undead Gladiator from your graveyard to your hand. Activate only during your upkeep.\\nCycling {1}{B} ({1}{B}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', '{1}{G}, Sacrifice Vessel of Nascency: Reveal the top four cards of your library. You may put an artifact, creature, enchantment, land, or planeswalker card from among them into your hand. Put the rest into your graveyard.', '{1}{G}, {T}, Discard a card: Creatures you control get +1/+1 and gain trample until end of turn.', '{1}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice Magus of the Wheel: Each player discards their hand, then draws seven cards.', '{1}{W}, Exile Dauntless Cathar from your graveyard: Create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{1}{W}{U}, {T}: Return target artifact or enchantment card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{2}, {T}: Copy target triggered ability you control. You may choose new targets for the copy. (A triggered ability uses the words "when," "whenever," or "at.")', '{2}: Put a plot counter on Deadly Designs. Any player may activate this ability.\\nWhen there are five or more plot counters on Deadly Designs, sacrifice it. If you do, destroy up to two target creatures.', '{2}: Target creature gains trample until end of turn. If this is the third time this ability has resolved this turn, you may add {R}{R}{R}{R}{R}{R}{R}{R}.', '{2}{U}, {T}, Sacrifice another creature: Reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a nonlegendary creature card. Put that card onto the battlefield and the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.', '{3}{G}: Knight of the Skyward Eye gets +3/+3 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', "{4}{U}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn.", '{8}: Target creature gets +5/+5 and gains trample until end of turn.', '{B}: Regenerate Twisted Abomination.\\nSwampcycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for a Swamp card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', '{G}, {T}: You may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield.', '{R}, {T}: Spikeshot Goblin deals damage equal to its power to any target.', '{R}: Chartooth Cougar gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\nMountaincycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for a Mountain card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', '{R}: Target creature you control gains haste until end of turn. (It can attack and {T} this turn.)', "{T}, Sacrifice Nihil Spellbomb: Exile target player's graveyard.\\nWhen Nihil Spellbomb is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, you may pay {B}. If you do, draw a card.", '{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only during your upkeep.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color.\\n{T}: Put a charge counter on Coalition Relic.\\nAt the beginning of your precombat main phase, remove all charge counters from Coalition Relic. Add one mana of any color for each charge counter removed this way.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\nBasic landcycling {1} ({1}, Discard this card: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\nMorph {2} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Tap target land.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}: Mishra's Factory becomes a 2/2 Assembly-Worker artifact creature until end of turn. It's still a land.\\n{T}: Target Assembly-Worker creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}: Each player draws a card.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}, Sacrifice Haunted Fengraf: Return a creature card at random from your graveyard to your hand.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{B/G}, {T}: Add {B}{B}, {B}{G}, or {G}{G}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{G/U}, {T}: Add {G}{G}, {G}{U}, or {U}{U}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{R/W}, {T}: Add {R}{R}, {R}{W}, or {W}{W}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Quicksand: Target attacking creature without flying gets -1/-2 until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{U/R}, {T}: Add {U}{U}, {U}{R}, or {R}{R}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{W/B}, {T}: Add {W}{W}, {W}{B}, or {B}{B}.', '{T}: Add {G}.\\n{T}: Target 1/1 creature gets +1/+2 until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {G}{G}{G}.\\nForestcycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Search your library for a Forest card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.)', '{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{T}: Draw two cards. Target opponent gains control of Humble Defector. Activate only during your turn.', '{T}: Target Assembly-Worker creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{T}: Untap target Forest.', '{U}: Untap Horseshoe Crab.', '{X}, Sacrifice Pernicious Deed: Destroy each artifact, creature, and enchantment with mana value X or less.']
flavor: ['"(Z—>)90° — (E—N²W)90°t = 1"', '"A boon from the angels should never be cast aside."\\n—Manfried Ulmach, Chief Inquisitor', '"A hedron holds magic for a thousand years—or less, if need be."', '"A river of lava is just another river to cross."', '"All are not equal—neither in life nor after death. Bontu\'s favorites will stand highest in eternity."\\n—Senifet, vizier of Bontu', '"Beauty to the eye does not always translate to the touch."\\n—Naimah, Femeref philosopher', '"Behold blessed perfection."\\n—Sheoldred, Whispering One', '"Brave scar or unfortunate tale? It all depends on your pain threshold."', '"Center of the Sea, Eye of the World, Shrine of Enlightenment. Seek it for answers. Seek it for healing. Seek it and return transformed."\\n—Scroll fragment from the ruins of Minamo', '"Do not linger in such places, child. There the gwyllions dance. If they find you, you will join in their revels for eternity."\\n—Talara, elvish safewright', '"Each night, the sun unravels and blows away. Each day, the spiders set a new one in the sky."\\n—Sunseeder myth', '"Eldrazi? Ha! Try walking through Zulaport at night with your pockets full. Now *that\'s* dangerous."', '"Even if we defeat it, what remains to be saved?"\\n—Glissa Sunseeker', '"Even storm clouds bow to worship Avacyn."\\n—Elder Rimheit', '"Even the threat of power has power."\\n—Jeska, warrior adept', '"Fate is not as fixed as you might think."', '"From Gaea grew the world, and the world was silent. From Gaea grew the world\'s elves, and the world was silent no more."\\n—Elvish teaching', '"Guilds be damned. We can fend for ourselves."\\n—Vennick of the Gateless', '"Here lies Gond, hero of Safehold Taldwen. May he ever guide our quest."', '"Humans use pigs to hunt for mushrooms, don\'t they? It\'s like that."\\n—Harak, Malakir bloodwitch', '"I am not afraid to die today nor afraid of what death will bring."', '"I do not miss Jukai Forest. It is not my home. My home is Kamigawa, its people my family. Wherever I set my pack and rest my head, I am home."', '"I have seen and heard much here. There are secrets within secrets. Let me show you."\\n—Takara, to Eladamri', '"I never thought I\'d spend my life fighting. I\'m a maker, not a destroyer."', '"In memories, we can find our deepest reserves of strength."', '"In the gathering there is strength for all who founder, renewal for all who languish, love for all who sing."\\n—*Song of All*, canto 642', '"It\'s rarely worth questioning where the mana comes from. Just be grateful."\\n—Jaya Ballard, task mage', '"It\'s right to fear those that you keep locked away."\\n—Rahilda, Vildin-Pack alpha', '"Leave no scraps, lest you attract pests."\\n—Mardu threat', '"Let nothing own the skies but the wind."\\n—Dejara, Giltwood druid', '"Life as we know it dangles on the brink of extinction. We must show the strength they would steal from us."\\n—*The Invokers\' Tales*', '"Many must die for the one who should not have perished."', '"Meat *and* eggs. We eat!"\\n—Borborygmos', '"No matter how busy my schedule gets, I always try to take time for that personal touch."\\n—Queen Marchesa', '"Of all the things that can be stolen, opportunity is the most valuable."', '"On dark nights you can still see the light of the Vess girl\'s lantern out in the Caligo, seeking her lost brother. Those who follow are doomed to join her endless search."\\n—"The Fall of the House of Vess"', '"On every plane, there are those who run toward danger."\\n—Gideon Jura', '"One alone is fearsome; one among many is unstoppable."\\n—Benalish proverb', '"Only the most effective tactics stand the test of time."\\n—Gamelen, Citanul elder', '"Proximity discouraged. Do not approach."\\n—Vulshok field guide', '"Rage courses in every heart, yearning to betray its rational prison."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"She knows every step of this coastline, both above and below the surface, and she has hideouts all along the way. She will get you there."\\n—Jori En, expedition leader', '"Such a lord as this—all virtues\' height—\\nHad never been, nor ever was again."', '"Terrifying, but thankfully temporary."\\n—Teferi', '"The Origin Query will wait. We must ensure we survive to return to it."\\n—Pelyus, vedalken ordinar', '"The battle is won. There\'s work to be done. / The Blessed Sleep must wait. / A fiend is about. It stalks the devout. / I\'ll save them from my fate."\\n—"The Good Geist\'s Vow"', '"The embers of our homes still smolder, and already the villages of Kjeldor burn in retaliation. What they have started, we will finish."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes', '"The enlightenment I never found in etherium I have found traced in the coatl\'s scales."\\n—Ranalus, vedalken heretic', '"The explorer who found it got a bad deal when he sold it. He merely got rich."', '"The first birth celebrates life. The second birth mocks it."\\n—Mystic elder', '"The harder they try to extinguish my faith, the brighter it burns in the darkness."', '"The need for the pack is bred in their bones. Their true strength will not show itself for any other purpose."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"The nezumi will do things for money no other thinking creature would consider. This, of course, makes them useful beyond words."\\n—Meloku the Clouded Mirror', '"The rules are clear. If you want to leave, you need only convince another to take your place."', '"The second wind of ascension is Reaver, slaying the unworthy."\\n—*Keld Triumphant*', '"The thunder of hooves is music to my ears."', '"The tools of evil are mere things. And like all things, they cannot last forever."\\n—*Song of All*, canto 881', '"There are no obstacles, only different paths."', '"There is great wisdom in rushing headlong into combat . . . if you\'re prepared."\\n—Kenjek, captain of the Thousand Swords', '"Thraben is our home and I will not see it fall to this unhallowed horde."', '"True strength is in the mind, for the body is too malleable a form."\\n—Politus, vedalken emisar', '"Twice I have let the Legacy slip away. Never again."\\n—Karn, silver golem', '"We earn no medals and fight for no titles. Blood is proof of our victory."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes', '"We wield the fires of rage. War is our blood and destruction our birthright."\\n—Crimson creed', '"When I said I needed a hand, I didn\'t mean this."\\n—Gerrard Capashen', '"Why do you weep for the dead? I rejoice, for they have died for me."', '"With his dream of unification fulfilled, Darien became the last king of Kjeldor. Those who followed were known as the kings of New Argive."\\n—*Kjeldor: Ice Civilization*', '"Wrath is no vice when inflicted upon the deserving."', '"Yawgmoth," Freyalise whispered as she set the bomb, "now you will pay for your treachery."', '"You can become anything if I just put my mind to it."', '"You know it to be false, but when its claws find you, what you know won\'t matter much at all."\\n—Pol Jamaar, illusionist', '"You were once Mardu, so your body and will are strong. Now we must train your mind."\\n—Houn, Jeskai elder', "A ghoulcaller's playground.", 'A passionate recruiter will win a war before the first arrow flies.', 'A single seed unleashes a flurry of growth.', "After years of world-bending machinations, Bolas's triumph is at hand.", "All Mirri wanted to do was rest, but she couldn't ignore a nagging suspicion as she followed Crovax's skulking form.", 'All seeds share a common bond, calling to each other across infinity.', "All the aether charts in the world can't compete with the trained eye of a talented scout.", "An ogre's poisonous stench is like fine Kashkaval cheese to the noses lowest to the ground.", 'Any pyromancer can summon fire with a thought. The trick is putting it out.', 'As Hedrax stepped into oblivion, he welcomed the unwavering silence.', 'As their roots soaked in a weak tea of bogwater and decay, the trees absorbed the essence of death into their living tissue.', 'At full moon, the river seeps over its banks and crawls through the woods like a blanket of serpents.', 'Boggarts and disturbing bits of boggarts flew through the air with alarming and untidy regularity.', "Chainer's dark gift to a darker soul.", 'Chandra never believed in using her "inside voice."', "Dominaria's most ancient evil.", 'Even among the hardiest warriors of the Temur, loxodons are respected for their adaptation to the mountain snows.', 'Even more than carrion, they crave the last words of the dying.', 'Fblthp had always hated crowds.', 'Fire burns away both flesh and freedom.', 'For the first time in his life, Grakk felt a little warm and fuzzy inside.', 'Going down with the ship is just the beginning.', 'Hatred outlives the hateful.', 'His prowess gives the guildless hope that they can hold out against tyranny.', 'His watch ends only when he does.', 'Hobs bury their kin far from home. They believe the dry, open ground keeps hags from stealing the bones and gwyllions from stealing the spirits.', 'Honor the gods of Theros, and they will return the favor.', 'Hope of deliverance is scorched by the fire of futility.', 'If only every message were as perfect as its bearer.', "If you feel the ground quake, run. If you hear its bellow, flee. If you see its teeth, it's too late.", "If you stare at the sun for too long, you'll lose your ability to see clearly.", 'In a withered world, the scent of healthy prey is enough to drive a predator to frenzy.', 'In the final days before the disaster, all the crabs on Tolaria migrated from inlets, streams, and ponds back to the sea. No one took note.', "Infested with vermin, ever hungering, dropping from night's sky.", 'It feeds on dry bones in the sand and desperate pleas in the wind.', 'It returns eager to share the feast of blood and gore with its ghoulish master.', 'It sees itself in all of its creations.', 'Its fangs are in your flesh before its hiss leaves your ears.', 'Its growl is the crackling and popping of a wildfire untamed.', 'Its tines cannot be rung by mere physical force. Only magic of great power can start its eldritch resonance.', "Keldon warriors don't need signals to tell them when to attack. They need signals to tell them when to stop.", 'Knowledge demands sacrifice.', 'Kongming and Lu Su tricked Wei troops into shooting over 100,000 arrows at them to later use against the Wei at Red Cliffs.', "Merfolk don't always know what they're looking for, but they're certain once they find it.", 'No matter how deep you bury it, some evil refuses to stay dead.', 'No matter the timeline, some legends will endure.', "No mortal could atone for Ihsan's betrayal. Redemption required him to become something else.", 'No tactic transforms a battle like a well-timed carnivore.', 'Not all deaths are etched with mythic meaning and iconic glory.', 'Nothing escapes a sharp mind.', 'Nothing lives within it, yet there is life.', 'Nothing restrains a burning passion.', "Once they reached Orazca, the Legion's explorers ransacked tombs and temples, hunting for the Immortal Sun.", 'Only in Ravnica do the wolves watch the flock.', 'Opening Orazca unleashed more horrors than just the Immortal Sun.', 'Phyrexia wastes nothing. Its food chain is a spiraling cycle.', 'Rishada is the gateway to free trade—but the key will cost you.', 'Saltfield nomads call a sudden storm a "whitemane."', 'Skepticism fades in the face of the miraculous.', 'Some corpses the Golgari cannot claim. Some souls the Orzhov cannot shackle.', 'The Cabal loves encores.', 'The Order of the Skyward Eye does the bidding of an evil force, unwittingly stirring fear and mistrust across Bant in accordance with his plans.', 'The best wishes include the will to tame their consequences.', "The clamor of war ceased as both armies stood and marveled at the beauty of Gaea's work.", 'The drums of war stir the hearts of all who fight for righteousness.', 'The dwarves call their quicksilver techniques "improvisational weaponsmithing."', "The executioner's tree in Thraben Cathedral holds the power to absolve more than the souls of the hanged.", 'The first morning after acquiring her familiar, the wizard awoke with fleabites and mange.', "The gods are fascinated by innocence, perhaps because it's a quality they themselves lack.", 'The kavu might be above you\\n—Llanowar expression meaning "keep an open mind"', 'The lacerators cut themselves before each hunt. They must feed before the sun rises or bleed to death.', 'The lamps on Wyndmoor Street snuff themselves at midnight and refuse to relight, afraid to illuminate what lies in the darkness.', 'The limbs of Pendelhaven extend as far as the meek roam, and reach as high as they strive.', "The most frightening storms are those not woven by nature's hand.", 'The passing of the sai presages the end of the old clan and the ascent of the new.', 'The sound of its plated tail beating on desert rocks is often mistaken for the footfalls of a much larger predator.', "The sparkmage shrieked, calling on the rage of the storms of his youth. To his surprise, the sky responded with a fierce energy he'd never thought to see again.", 'The spite of the Cabal turns meadow into mire.', "The upside to not thinking about the consequences is that you'll always surprise those who do.", 'The wills of mortals shift as the tide ebbs and flows.', 'Their eardrums may have given out, but the rest of them never will.', 'Their skills are extensive, and their appetite for battle just as vast.', "There's no stronger armor than the bravery of those beside you.", 'They lived in different nations and fought in different eras, but as the Returned, they link arms as one.', "They'll attack whatever's in front of them—as long as you tell them where that is.", 'Those who expect betrayal at every turn are seldom disappointed.', "Though Shadowmoor's monster-haunted wilds beckon, she never leaves her post.", 'To Mirrodin, an explosive. To Phyrexia, a missionary.', 'Travelers bathe in the falls to wash away curses from the pucas who lurk nearby.', 'Treefolk and elves share a common interest in the forests, but really the elves just feel at home with the view from above.', "Tribal rivalries and petty disputes were laid aside at Eladamri's summons.", 'Water calls to water, and the world is left exhausted and withered in its wake.', 'When a strong mind moves, form and energy shift to heed it.', 'When it walked, it altered geography. When it bellowed, it changed the weather.', "When provoked, a flamekin's inner fire burns far hotter than any giant's forge.", 'Where the geometries of the world collapse, a master of the aether can harvest power beyond comprehending.', 'Which is worse—the sleep which never ends or that which never comes?', 'While the smell of burning flesh is common in Grixis, the odor of smoldering brain matter is a rare treat.', "With their factories long destroyed, some of Mishra's creations still toil in remote areas, endlessly performing and reperforming their last orders.", 'Xenagos reveled while Theros burned.']
